@startuml User_Authentication_Data_Model
' Edison UPM - User model extended for authentication (Sprint 2, task #117)
' Login options:
'  - UPM community (Student, Professor, Administrator): UPM SSO only, no password stored
'  - Investor: self sign-up with email + password, email must be verified
' Existing columns of users (id, full_name, email, role) are kept, so ideas,
' comments and saved ideas that point to users.id keep working.

title Edison UPM - User Authentication Data Model (Sprint 2)

skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F1F1F1
  BorderColor #555555
  AttributeFontSize 11
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide circle
hide empty methods

class User <<users>> {
  id : UUID <<PK>>
  fullName : String {length <= 120}
  email : String {unique, length <= 254}
  role : UserRole
  .. new in Sprint 2 ..
  authMethod : AuthMethod
  passwordHash : String [0..1]
  emailVerified : Boolean
  status : AccountStatus
  failedLoginAttempts : Integer
  createdAt : DateTime
  lastLoginAt : DateTime [0..1]
}

class EmailVerificationToken <<email_verification_tokens>> {
  id : UUID <<PK>>
  tokenHash : String {unique}
  expiresAt : DateTime
  usedAt : DateTime [0..1]
  createdAt : DateTime
}

class RefreshToken <<refresh_tokens>> {
  id : UUID <<PK>>
  tokenHash : String {unique}
  expiresAt : DateTime
  revokedAt : DateTime [0..1]
  createdAt : DateTime
}

enum UserRole {
  STUDENT
  PROFESSOR
  ADMINISTRATOR
  INVESTOR
}

enum AuthMethod {
  UPM
  PASSWORD
}

enum AccountStatus {
  UNVERIFIED
  ACTIVE
  LOCKED
  DELETED
}

class "Idea / Comment / SavedIdea" as Existing <<Sprint 1>> {
  founder_id / author_id / user_id → users.id
}

User "1" *-down- "0..*" EmailVerificationToken : verifies email with
User "1" *-down- "0..*" RefreshToken : sessions
Existing "0..*" -up-> "1" User : unchanged

' keep enums grouped together below the classes
EmailVerificationToken -[hidden]down- UserRole
UserRole -[hidden]right- AuthMethod
AuthMethod -[hidden]right- AccountStatus

note right of User
  <b>Rules (checked by BACK)</b>
  authMethod = UPM
    → passwordHash null (user found by email)
    → role STUDENT, PROFESSOR or ADMINISTRATOR
    → emailVerified = true, status starts ACTIVE
  authMethod = PASSWORD
    → passwordHash required (BCrypt)
    → role INVESTOR
    → status starts UNVERIFIED until email verified
  5 failed password logins → status LOCKED
end note

note bottom of RefreshToken
  Only the hash of each token is stored.
  Access tokens are not stored (short-lived JWT).
end note
@enduml
